# Isolate Management Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for implementing robust isolate management to handle heavy tasks without affecting UI responsiveness. These principles apply to all background processing operations.

## Best Practices
- Implement self-healing isolates that recover from errors
- Design real-time progress reporting for long-running tasks
- Support task cancellation for user-initiated operations
- Implement automatic fallback to main thread for critical tasks
- Optimize data transfer between isolates
- Implement proper isolate lifecycle management
- Design prioritization mechanisms for concurrent tasks
- Track and report task metrics for performance analysis
- Implement proper error propagation from isolates

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize isolate management components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      isolates/
        isolate_manager.dart
        isolate_task.dart
        isolate_worker.dart
        isolate_progress.dart
        task_result.dart
        task_priority.dart
        isolate_exception.dart
      utils/
        isolate_data_converter.dart
    domain/
      usecases/
        process_in_background_usecase.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use descriptive task types: `IsolateTaskType.imageProcessing`
- Implement standardized result wrapper: `TaskResult<T>`
- Use enum for task priorities: `TaskPriority.critical`
- Implement proper progress reporting: `IsolateProgress(0.5, "Processing image")`
- Track task states with enums: `TaskState.queued`, `TaskState.processing`
- Use consistent naming conventions for isolate-related components
- Document memory usage expectations for different task types

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Use `Uint8List` for efficient transfer of large binary data
- Optimize serialization for complex objects
- Reuse isolates instead of creating new ones for each task
- Limit maximum concurrent isolates based on device capability
- Use SendPort/ReceivePort for efficient message passing
- Implement object pooling for frequent task types
- Schedule non-critical tasks during idle periods
- Monitor and log isolate performance metrics
- Implement Isolate Groups for related tasks when appropriate

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test recovery from isolate crashes
- Verify progress reporting accuracy
- Test task cancellation at different stages
- Validate memory usage during heavy processing
- Test concurrent execution of multiple isolates
- Verify proper resource cleanup after task completion
- Test with different data sizes to ensure robustness
- Benchmark performance with various task configurations
- Test fallback mechanism to main thread
